    readTitle: 'Why are qubits kept so cold?', readText: ['Qubits are the tiny parts that make a quantum computer work. They are very sensitive. Heat, light and even small vibrations can disturb them.', 'That is why scientists keep qubits in special fridges. These fridges are colder than outer space, just a tiny bit above the coldest temperature possible.', 'When a qubit is disturbed, it loses its special quantum mix. Keeping it cold helps it stay calm long enough to do its work.'],
